From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SamuriHL <samurihl@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:11:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vdec: program the slave stream write pointer on no-parser
 SoCs

With no stream parser (SC2 and S6 among them) only the master of a dual
layer pair writes HEVC_STREAM_WR_PTR. The slave copies the master's wp
into its vbuf and leaves the register at the master's last run. So
vdec_has_more_input stays true on the slave, and an el can spin at the
end of input.
---
 drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
@@ -0,6 +0,9 @@
 			} else {
 				STBUF_WRITE(&vdec->vbuf, set_wp,
 					STBUF_READ(&vdec->master->vbuf, get_wp));
+				/* the register still holds the master's last run */
+				WRITE_VREG(HEVC_STREAM_WR_PTR,
+					STBUF_READ(&vdec->vbuf, get_wp));
 			}
 		} else {
 			WRITE_VREG(HEVC_STREAM_WR_PTR,
